    "body": "<!-- pr-reviewer: 246d072275efced06ba67bf82871a64c7d856a6b -->\n**Verdict: Needs changes before merge** (one small process fix).\n\n**What looks good**\n- `set_tool_number` runs the existing undoable `SetToolNumber` through `env.history` (one undo step); refusals come back by name (unknown/non-tool, range 1-99999, duplicate, no-op, missing `number`). No unwrap/expect/panic; the u64 to u32 conversion is checked (`tool_number_tools.rs:41-43`).\n- `number` is required, so a missing field is refused rather than read as a clear. `get_job` gains `number` and `posts_as`; additive only. No posted-G-code logic changes (the Fanuc T17 check is in the pin test), so the safety floor does not apply.\n- Test lives in `crates/app/tests/` and imports app-defined MCP code. Files stay under 400 lines. Decision entry present, no new dependency, no snapshot PNGs, no UI change, Changelog and `Fixes #730` present.\n\n**Local results** (PR head; main `683802be` is already an ancestor, trial merge clean)\n- `mcp_tool_number`: 1 passed (the pinning test)\n- `mcp`: 19 passed; `mcp_edit_tool`: 3 passed; `mcp_holder`: 5 passed\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean\n\n**Requested before merge**\n1. `.claude/PROCESS_VERSION` is 48, but main is 46, so the bump must be 47 (`.claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/SKILL.md` is a process file). AGENTS.md: two open process PRs bump to the same number and the second to merge takes the next on its merge of main. Set it to 47.\n\n**Notes (not blocking)**\n- No script verb (named as dropped in the decision file); fine.\n- `job.rs` removes `tool` from the shared view helper's output by hand; a small helper split would be tidier.\n\nA maintainer will approve and merge by hand.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
